---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { about } from "../content";
import PageHero from "@dst/ui/PageHero.astro";
---
<Layout
  prose title={about.title} description={about.description}>
  <PageHero
    title={about.h1}
    image="/covers/about.jpg"
    imageAlt="Cut-paper illustration: a folded map of a wide river bend crossed by three bridges."
    imageKind="generated"
  >
    <p class="lede">{about.lede}</p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p set:html={`<strong>London Today</strong> covers central London — exhibitions, carnival, theatre and the weekend. What is on, and when it starts.`} />
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The rules</h2>
    <ol class="rules">
      <li>
        <h3>Every fact names where it came from, and when we last looked</h3>
        <p>Not &ldquo;updated regularly&rdquo;. A source and a date, printed on the entry itself, so you can see how fresh the thing you are reading actually is.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Nothing is listed on a date we could not confirm</h3>
        <p>Dates come from the organiser, not from another listings page. An event whose date we could not confirm waits until we can.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>What&rsquo;s on, not what went wrong</h3>
        <p>This site covers what is happening, what is open and what changed for the better. Not politics, not crime, not tragedy, and not arguments. If a story needs a side taken, it belongs somewhere that can follow it up.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>We pick the best, and say why</h3>
        <p>A listings site earns its keep by choosing. Picking out the best of something is the job, not a compromise &mdash; what it will not do is run a place down. A takedown of a named business is not what this is for.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A page exists when there is something to put on it</h3>
        <p>No empty sections waiting to be filled, and no index padded out to look busy. A section appears once there is something on it.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="container" id="statistics">
    <h2>Statistics and cookies</h2>
    <p>We count visits with Google Analytics, and only if you agree. Until you have answered, and if you decline, Google Analytics is not loaded at all: it sets no cookies and receives no data. The site works the same either way.</p>
    <p>If you allow it, Google Analytics sets cookies (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_…</code>, kept for up to two years) so that it can tell when the same browser comes back. Google then learns which pages you open and which links you follow, the kind of device and browser you use and, worked out from your IP address, roughly where you are. That includes the page you were on when you answered, and what you clicked on it before answering. Google processes this data, including on servers in the United States. We use it for totals: how often a page was read and where its visits came from. The advertising features of Google Analytics are switched off.</p>
    <p>Your answer is kept in this browser and stands for <span class="nowrap">180 days</span>, after which we ask again. You can change it whenever you like, here or under &ldquo;Cookie settings&rdquo; at the foot of every page. If you later decline, counting stops and the cookies are deleted at once; visits already counted stay in the totals.</p>
    <p><button class="button button-secondary" type="button" data-consent-open title="Change whether we count your visits">Cookie settings</button></p>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .rules {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: rule;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .rules li {
    counter-increment: rule;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
    gap: 0 var(--space-2);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .rules li::before {
    content: counter(rule);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .rules h3 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .rules p { margin: 0.25em 0 0; grid-column: 2; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
